The output from this program is the same as the previous example.

@image html date_example02.png

@section ww_date_unix Writing Unix datetimes

Another alternative when handling dates is [Unix Time](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time)
which is a common integer time format. It is defined as the number of seconds since the Unix epoch
(1970-01-01 00:00 UTC).

The `worksheet_t::write_unixtime()` function can be used to write dates and times
in this format. Negative values can also be used for dates prior to 1970:

@dontinclude dates_and_times03.cpp
@skip include
@until }

The output from this program is:

@image html date_example03.png

